  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/motion/src/turning/offset.rs`: the line claim of a profile segment now holds only over its claim window. In that window the tangent point of the ball is on the segment. The claim window is the segment's station window, shifted by `d*b/sqrt(1 + b^2)`. At other stations, the circle about the nearer end point makes the claim.\n- The OD ride (`profile_offset`) and the bore ride (`profile_offset_in`) use the same rule, through one private helper (`seg_claims`, `SegClaim`, `seg_range`).\n- `seg_range` replaces the old probe of the ±1 neighbour segments. A shifted window can reach past the next segment.\n- The two catalog programs `turning/cone-thread` and `turning/contour-finishes` are regenerated.\n- `docs/decisions/2881-offset-tangent-window.md` records the decision.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe old code held the infinite offset line of a segment over the segment's own station window. This is wrong in two directions:\n\n- A steep, short chord claimed its line far above the bar. The first chord of a fillet has a slope of 16.6, so the claim was 167 mm too high (X354 on a 30 mm bar).\n- A sloped face did not claim the stations before its inside corner, where it is the nearest piece. There the ride stood nearer than `d` to the face. This is a small gouge into the leave (0.884 instead of 1.0 at a 45 degree corner in the pin).\n\n## Tests\n\nNew suite `crates/motion/tests/turning_offset_window.rs`. Each test checks that every ride sample stands at exactly `d` from the profile:\n\n- `a_steep_fillet_chord_keeps_the_ride_on_the_nose`: before the fix the max ride radius was 28.29 on an 11.66 profile.\n- `a_sloped_inside_corner_is_not_gouged`: before the fix the ride stood 0.884 from the face at station -0.25.\n- `the_inside_ride_obeys_the_same_window`: before the fix the bore ride dived to r 1.71 on an 18.34 wall.\n\nMutation checks:\n\n- Old `offset.rs` put back: all 3 pins red. Restored: all 3 green.\n- Sign of the window shift flipped: all 3 pins red. Restored: all 3 green.\n\nGate:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (motion lib, `turning_bore`, `turning_offset_window`, `turning_prof`, app `example_catalog`).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Also run green in debug: app suites `turning_profile`, `turning_bore`, `turning_bore_feeds`, `turning_contour`, `turning_contour_stock`, `turning_axial_rapids`, `turning_stock_approach`, `turning_hidden_floor`, `turning_insert_zone`, `turning_holder`, `turning_holder_steel`, `lathe_post`, `lathe_post_tormach`, `lathe_post_turn_radius`, `lathe_stroke`, `lathe_field_sim`, `recorded_post_streams`, `coarse_laws`, `coarse_rims`, `sim_lathe_body`, `ladder_entry_height`, `carried_stock_entry`, `stepped_stock_rapid`, `project_roundtrip`.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nTwo `.nc` files. The `.camproj` files do not change: the catalog tests pass with the committed projects.\n\n- `examples/catalog/turning/cone-thread/cone-thread.nc`: at the cone-to-flat inside corner (Z59.2), each rough rung and the finish ride lose a run of zero-length `G01` blocks and a vertical drop. The new ride rolls over the corner on the nose circle (for example `G01 X28.532 Z59.697`, then `X28.5 Z60.194`). It stands slightly farther out than the old drop, which was inside the true offset.\n- `examples/catalog/turning/contour-finishes/contour-finishes.nc`: near Z0 to Z1 the rides lose about 50 short blocks each that went out toward the spike of a steep chord. The clearance radius drops from `X22.884` to `X21.6`, and from `X20.762` to `X20.1` for the chamfer. The chamfer retract is now a short feed out to X20.1, then the rapid. The operation's own lead-out law makes this choice for the new, nearer clearance.\n\nNo other `.nc` or `.cl` golden changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The heavy lanes. `cargo xtask gate heavy` reaches every app and motion heavy target for a change in `motion`. These were not run. Run them before the PR is flagged ready.\n- The exact model of the issue (30 mm bar, 1.2 mm fillet). The pin uses the same chord slope in a hand-made profile.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #2897 (#2882) touches `crates/motion/src/turning/offset.rs`: the same file, different function (`thin`, and the final `Ok(...)` lines). It also regenerates `examples/catalog/turning/cone-thread/cone-thread.nc`. Whichever merges second refreshes and regenerates that golden.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: Turning profile rough and finish no longer ride far out of the bar at a steep fillet chord, and no longer ride inside the nose offset at a sloped inside corner.\n\nFixes #2881\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
